@startuml 22-scenario-simulation
skinparam backgroundColor #F7F8FA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Aptos
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ArrowColor #566173
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #168B80
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #E6F4F1
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #4969C5
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #EAF0FF
skinparam ActorBorderColor #D88A16
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFF4E5

actor "Mall manager" as manager
participant "Atlas Twin UI" as ui
database "Current twin state" as twin
participant "Scenario engine" as sim
participant "Movement + congestion\nmodels / agents" as models
participant "Comparison + explanation" as compare

manager -> ui : Ask: “What if Entrance 2 closes?”
ui -> twin : Read current baseline
twin --> ui : Live state + confidence + freshness
ui -> sim : Create sandbox scenario\nclose entrance_2
sim -> sim : Fork current twin state\napply closure constraint
sim -> models : Run redistributed movement
models -> models : Estimate route changes\nzone pressure + dwell impact
models --> sim : Simulated trajectories + metrics
sim -> compare : Compare scenario vs baseline
compare --> ui : Impact map + explanation\nassumptions + uncertainty
ui --> manager : Show likely redistribution\nAtrium + Entrance 3 pressure

opt manager approves a real-world test
  manager -> ui : Approve bounded intervention
  ui -> ui : Record approval + scenario version
  ui -> twin : Send authorised action request
else manager does not approve
  manager -> ui : Save scenario for review
end

note over sim, compare
Simulation changes a virtual copy first.
It does not mutate live twin state or mall systems until
an explicitly authorised action is issued.
end note
@enduml
